{%- comment -%}
  Works out the live state of a competition and renders nothing.

  Because `render` isolates scope, this snippet is only used where its *output*
  is wanted. Callers that need the values compute them inline — see
  competition-card.liquid and sections/main-competition.liquid.

  This file documents the shared rules in one place so they stay consistent:

  OPEN        product.available and (no closing date, or closing date in future)
  CLOSING     open, and closing date is today or tomorrow
  FULL        not product.available because every entry has been bought
  CLOSED      closing date has passed
  UNAVAILABLE not available for any other reason (draft, unpublished variant)

  Metafields read (all optional, namespace `custom`):
    closing_at              date_time   entries close
    draw_at                 date_time   draw takes place
    entries_total           integer     entries released
    entries_sold            integer     entries taken
    prize_value             money       retail value of the prize
    cash_alternative        money       cash instead of the prize
    max_entries_per_person  integer     per-person cap
    instant_win             boolean     has instant win prizes
    competition_type        text        e.g. "Live draw"
    badge_label             text        one merchant-defined badge

  Nothing here invents a value. Each display is skipped when its metafield is
  empty, rather than falling back to a placeholder number.
{%- endcomment -%}
